				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				149,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Include active view column in editor state push to Mountain\n\nThe `sky:editor:activeChanged` and `sky:editor:selectionChanged` IPC payloads were hardcoded to `viewColumn: 1`, causing extensions querying `window.activeTextEditor.viewColumn` to always receive column 1 regardless of the actual editor group position.\n\nAdd a `GetViewColumn()` helper that reads `EditorGroups.activeGroup.index` (0-based) and converts to the 1-based view column expected by the VS Code extension API. The helper safely falls back to 1 when the EditorGroups service isn't yet available.\n\nExtensions relying on the active editor's view column now receive the correct value matching the editor's position in the group layout.",
			"SHA": "e5027bde2baa99b1829b51d01d8729017de3c6da"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:20:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				149,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Extract inline bridge handlers into dedicated module files\n\nReplace ~2500 lines of inline handler registrations in `Bridge.ts` with dynamic imports to four new dedicated module files, each owning a cohesive set of IPC channels:\n\n- `InstallWebview.ts`: Webview create/set-html/updateView/postMessage, WebviewView registration with workbench `IWebviewViewService` resolver chain, custom editor capability registration and disposal.\n- `InstallEditorOperations.ts`: Decoration set-ranges, text edits (`editor.edit()`), active editor / selection state push to Mountain, and `revealRange` scrolling.\n- `InstallTreeView.ts`: Tree view data provider attach (`TreeViewByViewId`), `ProvideChildren` via `MountainIPCInvoke`, exponential backoff retry chain, pending-attach queue for late-registering extensions, and DOM `cel:tree-view:*` event listeners.\n- `InstallUiRequests.ts`: Four show-message / show-input-box / show-quick-pick / show-message-with-actions request channels that require `ResolveUIRequest` round-trips to Mountain.\n\nEach module receives only the dependencies it needs (`Register`, `GetServices`, `Invoke`, `ApplyHtmlToWebview`, `ShowNotification`, `ResolveUiRequest`) via a thin injector interface, eliminating global-scope closure capture across unrelated handlers. The decomposition also simplifies per-module type definitions — previously all handler types were implicitly Any-typed from the inline closure chain.\n\nMinor side-effects:\n- `InstallDiagnostics.ts` and `InstallSearch.ts` get light formatting cleanup (single-line collapsed type annotations, removal of unused `Register` parameter) without behavioral change.\n- `ApplyHtmlToWebview` now loads eagerly in the bridge lifecycle (before any import call) so it's available for InstallWebview's registration callback, with a `globalThis.__CEL_WEBVIEW_APPLY_HTML__` stash for late-bound workbench resolvers.\n\nThe bridge's observable behaviour is unchanged: every registered channel fires the same handler logic as before, just from a dedicated module source file.",
			"SHA": "47d08be5e4485f258d9bea1890f46bda357927a1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:06:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				145,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat: Implement Sky Bridge for Diagnostics, SCM, and Search\n\n- Added InstallDiagnostics.ts to bridge diagnostics from Mountain to IMarkerService, enabling error visibility in the editor.\n- Introduced InstallScm.ts to handle SCM events, allowing Sky-side viewlets to mirror SCM state and register providers against the live workbench service.\n- Created InstallSearch.ts to register a search result provider that routes search queries to Mountain's handlers, ensuring proper file and text search functionality.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "c6982bf52f64f2f9ef7a60e23743af8ba103ca2d"
		},
